Hi Mike,

Thanks for all your work on the new version and commitment to the googlegroup!

I'm just running some tests on newly downloaded era5 data based on the micro_ncep() help file. My code is pasted below.
At two points the code breaks as it looks for the file in the wrong location.
1.  request_era5() downloaded the files fine, but couldn't find them when it went to combine them into combine.nc <http://combine.nc> (default combine = TRUE)
Error in nc_open trying to open file era5_2020.nc <http://era5_2020.nc> (return_on_error= FALSE )
2. micro_era5() couldn't find the files
Error in nc_open trying to open file C:/Users/ash/era5_data_2020.nc <http://era5_data_2020.nc> (return_on_error= FALSE )

I think the latter is due to code at line 750 in https://github.com/mrke/NicheMapR/blob/3.2.1/R/micro_era5.R

if(length(years)==1){
hourlydata <- mcera5::extract_clim(nc = paste0(spatial, '_', years, '.nc'), long = loc[1], lat = loc[2],
start_time = st_time, end_time = en_time)

The paste() would work for me if it had the file_prefix from build_era5_request() e.g
paste0(spatial, '/', file_prefix, '_', years, '.nc')
[1] "C:/Users/ash/era5_data/era5_2020.nc <http://era5_2020.nc>"
Obviously this doesn't work if file_prefix isn't in the R environment and you don't need to run build_era5_request() everytime you run micro_era5()
Not sure if I'm missing something or what the solution is in context of the rest of the code. Make file_prefix an argument in micro_era5() or use a list.files() call to get the file prefix from the file names?
Is the nichemapr preference for .nc files as individual years? If yes, maybe the request_era5() call should have a combine = FALSE argument.

Thanks again,

Ash

